// REJECTS: Unexpected token '::'. Valid alternatives: ['(']
//
// Filter, MultiGrainFilter and Join take a plain `identifier` as their name, NOT a
// qualifiedName. Their names are scoped to the enclosing Database, so `fixture::neg::Active`
// is not a longer name for a filter -- it is not a name at all.
//
// Everything else at this level of the file IS a qualified name: the Database itself, every
// `include`, every database pointer `[a::b::C]`. A rewrite with one identifier routine used
// everywhere accepts the package path here and produces a Database whose filters cannot be
// referenced by either engine.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::QualifiedFilterName
(
   Table T (ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY, VAL VARCHAR(32))
   Filter fixture::neg::Active(T.VAL = 'x')
)
